I committed this as Part of #1073, not "Fixes". The three readers the plan named now count sub-agent spend, and so does a fourth it missed (/tokens). One item on the issue's list is still own-spend only, so the issue stays open. Build, test, clippy, fmt, extract_trajectory.py --test and tests/harness_logic.sh all pass.

What changed (f41e50fe):
• `--output-format json`: a run that delegates now has a separate sub_agents object, the same shape as the audit usage record. Its cost_usd is null when delegated spend has no price. The existing usage and cost_usd still mean the run's own spend. A run that doesn't delegate has no new key and its output is unchanged; a test compares the whole object to check that.
• Delegated spend is still taken exactly once per run: audit_log_usage now takes it first and returns it, and the json output uses that same value. A real-binary test checks that the json output and the audit record report the same sub-agent spend, which would fail if anything emptied it a second time.
• `--cost-warn`: the running total now adds own and delegated spend before checking the threshold (record_run_costs). Delegated spend with no price is counted as an unpriced run, never as $0. The test covers a case that crosses the threshold only with delegation, the same case without delegation (no warning), and an unpriced child.
• `/tokens`: prints the same sub-agent lines /cost already shows; nothing extra without delegation. I added it because the issue's full comment lists it. There is no new test for this one: the lines come from a helper that already has tests, and the new code is just the call.
• `scripts/extract_trajectory.py`: phase totals now include sub_agents.cost_usd and show that part separately. A sub-agent record with tokens but no price is named, never added as $0. The "totals are a floor" line was reworded to what is still true. It adds about 70 bytes to the output, which is about 5.1 KB against its 6144-byte limit.
• I updated docs/src/features/cost-tracking.md and added a "superseded" note to ARCHITECTURE.md.

Checks that the tests can fail: I disabled the json change and the script's sub-agent sum one at a time, then put them back. Each made its tests fail by name (the json test, and four phase-spend rows), and each went green again once restored.

Still open on #1073: the per-turn breakdown in /cost still shows only each turn's own spend. Fixing it means deciding which turn a delegation is charged to. That depends on whether the saved message history keeps the tool result's sub-agent stats, which I haven't checked.

